# Environment and commands

Run commands from the project root, where `manage.py` and `compose.yaml` live,
regardless of the site source directory. Run Python, Django, tests, and formatters
inside the Docker `web` service by default. Use local UV commands when the user
has chosen local development; do not silently switch environments after a failure.
Git commands and Git hook installation run on the host.

Follow the README for `.env` setup; preserve an existing `.env`. Prepare Docker:

```shell
docker compose build
docker compose run --rm web uv sync --locked
```

One-off commands work without starting the web server; Compose starts required
database dependencies. To run the site, use `make docker`. With an already running
web service, `docker compose exec web uv run ...` is an alternative to
`docker compose run --rm web uv run ...`.

```shell
docker compose run --rm web uv run python manage.py makemigrations
docker compose run --rm web uv run python manage.py migrate
docker compose run --rm web uv run python manage.py test
```

Use `docker compose run --rm web uv add PACKAGE` or `uv remove PACKAGE` with the
same Compose prefix to manage dependencies; use `uv add --dev PACKAGE` for
development tools. Keep `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock` together in the change. Do
not maintain `requirements.txt` or install packages with pip. Prefer existing
libraries and the standard library to new dependencies. Rebuild the image when
its dependencies or system packages change; sync the container environment from
the lockfile when dependencies change.

For the user-selected local workflow, run `make sync` first.
{% if database != "sqlite3" %}Start the database with `make database`. Use `DATABASE_HOST=127.0.0.1` for local
Django commands and the credentials/port configured in `.env`; Make targets load
that file, but direct shell commands require those variables in the environment.
{% endif %}Replace `docker compose run --rm web uv run` with `uv run` for local
checks in [checks.md](checks.md). `make dev` runs locally and applies migrations;
`make check` runs local lint/format checks and tests, but does not include the
explicit system and
missing-migration checks in that guide.
